  <p>A knowledge graph is supposed to represent what is <em>known</em> so that it can be shared, combined, queried, and extended without corruption. Every knowledge-graph technology built over the past twenty-five years — RDF triples, OWL ontologies, Neo4j property graphs, and vector RAG databases — stores <strong>bare assertions</strong>. None of them represents <em>knowing</em>. An edge <code>(A, causes, B)</code> merely asserts that a relation holds; it carries no proof of derivation, no observation fiber on which it is valid, no contradiction detector, and no law governing how two edges compose.</p>

  <p>In Hyperactivity, the real basis of rational lawful evolution and information flow is a <strong>proof-theoretic knowledge graph</strong> whose geometry is a <strong>cubical cell complex</strong> and whose dynamics are a lock-free <strong>interaction network</strong> (<code>src/core.h</code>, <code>src/net.c</code>, <code>lib/check.hypercubical</code>):</p>

